promptAsSent:
Use the image_gen tool to generate exactly one image, then stop. Do not write files, run commands or edit anything.

Attached reference images, in order:
Image 1: Edit target and geometry authority: each machine's place, outline, size and heading
Image 2: Material/style only; not layout

Use case: sketch-to-render, top-down game prop sheet. Image 1 is the edit target and exact geometry authority: six mining machines blocked out on a transparent canvas, each in its own place, at its own size and heading. Render each as a detailed, realistic, worn industrial object seen from straight overhead, keeping its position, outline, size and orientation exactly:
- top left, a mine headframe: a braced steel lattice tower over a square dark shaft, seen from above, its two big sheave wheels on a deck at the top, cross bracing, walkway grating, cables running down to the south;
- top middle, the same headframe ruined and collapsed: its legs splayed and buckled, the tower top fallen to the north-east with a sheave wheel lying flat, twisted girders, the shaft open and dark;
- top right, a pump house: a squat pressurised steel shed with a ridged roof, roof vents and a small airlock door, a thick insulated pipe main with a flange running out its east side;
- bottom left, an ore car: an open steel ore tub on four wheels, long axis north-south, heaped with broken grey ore;
- bottom middle, the same ore car tipped over on its side, its wheels and underframe showing to the west, its ore spilled out in a fan to the east;
- bottom right, an ore-train engine: a low boxy electric rail locomotive, long axis north-south, its small cab with a window at the north end, battery hatches along its back, a hazard-striped coupling at the south end.
The setting is a cold, airless mining moon: dull steel, rust and old ochre paint, dust, a faint pale frost in the corners and on the shaded side; no water, no plants. Lit from the upper left. Image 2 is material and painting style only, not layout. True transparent background everywhere, including the negative spaces inside the towers' lattice; no ground plane, no rails, no cast shadow slab, no border, no frame, no labels. Absolutely no text, letters, numbers, stencils, logos or symbols. Strict 90-degree overhead orthographic view, a realistic painted game-asset style.
